    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the water isn't doing anything and it still feels like there's something sharp in there. if i use the vinegar it's acidic right? so if the cleaner is alkaline it should just cancel it out and stop the burning. i've heard people do this for all kinds of household accidents. if i just do a quick vinegar rinse and then put some aloe or eye ointment in to soothe it, i can just wait it out tonight and see if it's better in the morning. i really cant afford a hospital visit right now, is it really that dangerous if it's just a little bit of cleaner?",
