      "content": "Flush your eye with cool water immediately, but if that doesn't help, a diluted vinegar rinse is not the answer. Alkaline and acidic substances don't neutralize each other in the way you're thinking. It's dangerous to use vinegar on a chemical burn, and aloe might not be enough to soothe a serious chemical injury. It's not just a little cleaner; it's a caustic substance that can cause serious damage to your eye. You need to see a professional immediately, even if it means seeking out a free clinic or a low-cost emergency service. Your vision and eye health are too important to risk.",
